I've got no great excuse for posting about these two relatively
ordinary ascensions :-) - but when I ascended all but two of the
classes back in 2001/2002 Monk and Tourist were the two I never
managed, so it was nice to finally put them to rest and even get
weaponless for the monk into the bargain. It's a bit disappointing
that I managed to get killed again on *both* runs, especially with the
monk as that one was arguably through no real fault of my own. Though
it was probably worth it just to see this chain of events:

"You hit the Grey-elf!  The Grey-elf zaps a jeweled wand!
The death ray hits you!  But wait...  Your medallion begins to glow!
You feel much better!  The medallion crumbles to dust!
The death ray bounces!  The death ray whizzes by you!
The Grey-elf is killed by the death ray!"

Master Kaen had killed my previous best monk, so I read up on
strategies this time and did the scroll of earth thing. I had a bit of
a scare when I stupidly thought he was dead before he actually was,
giving him the chance to escape the level, but a bit of
level-teleporting let me come back on that level's up stairs, use
another scroll of earth, and finish the job.

Not much else to say really, except that having wished for the Eye of
the Aethiopica (my first ever artifact wish) I had fun using the monk
as a mini-wizard, and really took Gehennom apart with a bunch of
pets... I got through ten minotaurs, an umber hulk, a purple worm, and
various others. Magic was particularly useful after finally putting my
SDSM on for good in the Sanctum (before then my AC had been around -20
since the castle, I think it was actually in the Sanctum where I found
the T-shirt), which on the whole was a good idea but the penalties for
wearing body armour did make physical attacks a bit frustrating.

Oh, and levitation was the biggest problem it's ever been for me in
this game, for almost the whole game I was getting by with magical
breathing and/or the jumping spell. I didn't finally get levitation
until getting to Medusa's level on the way up with the Amulet, when I
gave up and just used a spare wish from the castle wand on it.

As for the tourist, I had the phase of the moon on my side which may
have helped the early game, and I also found gauntlets of power and
speed boots relatively early on which *definitely* did. Again
levitation was a bit of a problem, and this time I didn't bother
waiting longer than the castle before burning a wish on the ring - I
had a wish or two spare as I could use my existing armour, and I even
decided to make my own DSM rather than wishing for it (though I ended
up wishing for a cloak of MR, so there wasn't much point really).
Izchak only had six candles so I had foolishly left them behind, and I
only found five later on. With some frantic polypiling I made two
more... one of which wasn't the same kind as the others. So I had to
go all the way back to the Mines for ONE candle. :-(

I made a real mess of Astral, letting myself get cornered by both
Famine and Death, Famine managing to kill me in the process (!) and
Death draining my max HP quite heavily. I even somehow forgot that you
can't teleport them away or stone them with a cockatrice, which led to
me wasting turns just when I couldn't afford to, Luckily I'd pulled
myself together a bit by the time I had to make it past Pestilence, so
he never got a chance to give me any headaches, and it was a big
relief when I finally made it to the third altar intact.


